    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Past or perfect",
     "texto": [
      "Just as in English:\n\n- **Past** (spiste) = action at a moment in the past: I aftes **spiste** vi kl. 19. (Last night we ate at 7.)\n- **Perfect** (har spist) = the result matters now: Jeg er ikke sulten, for jeg **har spist**. (I'm not hungry: I've already eaten.)\n- **Pluperfect** (havde spist) = before another past event: Jeg **havde læst** bogen, så jeg kunne gå til eksamen. (I had read the book, so I could sit the exam.)\n\n⚠️ Watch out: with «for X time and still» Danish uses the perfect, just like English: Jeg **har boet** her i tre år (I've lived here for three years)."
     ],
     "tutora": "pensando"
    }
